SUMMARY
Learn clustering and attribution by analyzing multiple intrusions against a fictitious research company called EnvolveLabs. This is a good example of ways attribution can be challenging.
- How to apply foundational security analysis skills to analyze security log data
- How to “pivot” between datasets using indicators or patterns of interest
- How to identify tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs) based on observed threat activity
- How to cluster patterns of threat activity based on overlaps in adversary tradecraft and TTPs

SOURCE
https://kc7cyber.com/challenges/29

STEPS TAKEN
Section 1: KQL 101
How many employees are in the company?
Employees
| count
Answer: 1001

Which employee has the IP address: 192.168.0.191?
Employees
| where ip_addr == "192.168.0.191"
Answer: Mary Cook

How many emails did Laura Parrish receive?
let laura_email=
Employees
| where name =="Laura Parrish"
| project email_addr;
Email
| where recipient in (laura_email)
| count
Answer: 9

How many Envolve Labs employees received emails with the term vaccine in the subject?
Email
| where subject contains "vaccine"
| where recipient contains "envolvelabs.com"
| distinct recipient
Answer: 676

How many distinct urls did Keith Floyd visit?
let keith_ip=
Employees
| where name == "Keith Floyd"
| project ip_addr;
OutboundBrowsing
| where src_ip in (keith_ip)
| distinct url
Answer: 6

How many domains in the PassiveDns records contain the word vaccine?
PassiveDns
| where domain contains "vaccine"
| distinct domain
Answer: 7

What IP did the domain vaccine.net resolve to?
PassiveDns
| where domain == "vaccine.net"
| project ip
Answer: 58.235.85.30

How many unique URLs were browsed by employees named Karen?
let karen_ips=
Employees
| where name contains "Karen"
| project ip_addr;
OutboundBrowsing
| where src_ip in (karen_ips)
| distinct url
Answer: 43


